          "path": "_m/g/b/v/r/cockington-court-wp/cockington-court-cricket-pitch.jpg",
          "filename": "Cockington Court Cricket Pitch - geograph.org.uk - 49773.jpg",
          "caption": "Cockington Court Cricket Pitch. From the village Cockington Court can be reached by several routes. This one over the wooden walkway crosses the cricket pitch that is surely unique in that it sits in a veritable \"bowl\". The pavilion is high on the hillside to the right and I think all of the boundaries are higher than the batsmen. I can't imagine any Test Matches will ever be played here!",
